{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/166347-sheogorath-s-changeling-courts","id":166347,"title":"Sheogorath's Changeling Courts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-11T17:00:12-07:00","id":166347,"title":"Sheogorath's Changeling Courts","content":"I just had a crazy idea (pun intended) that combines Sheogorath from Elderscrolls with CtL: What if we had a changeling game where the freehold was divided into the Courts of Mania and Dementia? I don't know how you'd do it, but it'd be fucking amazing. Especially since this image inspired me on what the current monarch would look like. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://th06.deviantart.net/fs70/PRE/f/2012/360/6/c/sheogorath_by_feraurshiro_team-d5p9a3f.png\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://th06.deviantart.net/fs70/PRE/f/2012/360/6/c/sheogorath_by_feraurshiro_team-d5p9a3f.png\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://th06.deviantart.net/fs70/PRE/f/2012/360/6/c/sheogorath_by_feraurshiro_team-d5p9a3f.png\" target=\"_blank\"> http://th06.deviantart.net/fs70/PRE/f/2012/360/6/c/sheogorath_by_feraurshiro_team-d5p9a3f.png </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T17:24:21-07:00","id":166375,"title":"","content":"Been a while since I read much about it, but if I recall correctly the courts were meant to be symbols of stability.<br /> <br /> If that's true it might fit better for entitlements. I know vampires and werewolves have mania and dementia based subsplats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T17:44:49-07:00","id":166397,"title":"","content":"Ah, but what if it WASN'T a normal court, hm? What if Sheogorath was a Gentry who grew curious and/or jealous of the Changeling freeholds to the point he tried to replicate one within Arcadia, eg within his domain: the Shivering Isles?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T17:58:16-07:00","id":166403,"title":"","content":"That'd fit better, I think. It's not unique enough to mess with the 'Gentry not being able to create new things' rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T18:16:13-07:00","id":166415,"title":"","content":"You could actually make Kindly Ones of all the Deadric Princes, if you think about it. God help me if I know the exact stats for each or any of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T18:17:30-07:00","id":166416,"title":"","content":"The courts are indeed symbols of stability, and in fact, are aligned to aspects of Earth the True Fae can't understand. (It's in the core, page 45, in fact!) Madness is... not something you can use. And monarchs share their power, which is another detail that's important. It's why even a changeling taking major control of an area without sharing it in any way (like Grandfather Thunder in Miami, again in the core) is such a Bad Thing.<br /> <br /> Now. I haven't played Elder Scrolls, and um, can't say I'm impressed with the idea. At all. I'm disabled, and no, a game circling around that would not be amazing. In fact, it'd be something I'd slap someone over, because it's sure to be a piece of utterly inaccurate bull-hooey (even with research, because guess what? Mania and dementia develop and manifest themselves differently in different people!) and not to mention, well... Mania and dementia are real psychological conditions that real people suffer from, and they are not diametrically opposed. If you want to focus the courts on something other than the Seasons, you can do that, but don't bring real mental illness into it without at least knowing what you're talking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1989-astrakiseki","name":"AstraKiseki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1989_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T18:20:06-07:00","id":166418,"title":"","content":"...You do realize that nobody's making fun of anyone here, right? Or are you intentionally trying to stir the shit?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T18:38:44-07:00","id":166425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/166347-sheogorath-s-changeling-courts?p=166418#post166418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...You do realize that nobody's making fun of anyone here, right? Or are you intentionally trying to stir the shit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I do understand where Astra's coming from. People tend to throw around terms relating to disabilities, particularly mental disabilities, without much particular consideration for individuals who have to deal with those disabilities on a day-to-day basis. You may not be <i>deliberately</i> insulting anyone, but that's kind of the problem: you're using very loaded terminology without consideration of the implications of that terminology, and when someone calls you out on your carelessness, you cast the blame on <i>them</i> for daring to be offended at something very dear and personal to them. That's kind of backwards, to say the least.<br /> <br /> Now, I'm of two minds on the name. On the one hand, it seems like you're going for something like the traditional Seelie/Unseelie divide, which... well, you might as well just call them Seelie and Unseelie. On the other, you could just go whole hog and make the courts about extreme emotions and mental illness: the Dementia court is about the degradation of the mind and the descent into insanity, the Mania court is about mindless indulgence and acting without thinking, the Melancholia court is about endless contemplation and existential despair, and the Obsession court is about locking yourself into cycles of thought that you can't escape from. Of course, I don't know if you'd want to go there, but if you're going to pull out the loaded terminology, might as well go all the way, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T12:07:13-07:00","id":167128,"title":"","content":"But I didn't CHOOSE the name for the courts. If you actually played the Elder Scrolls, then you'd know that's what they are called. I just find it a hypocracy that people're getting offended at me for not having background information on the subject, when they themselves have no background information on what I'm talking about (eg the game). Besides, from an ingame perspective, what member of the Gentry would care if something appeared crass or offensive? They're evil!<br /> <br /> I digress. The whole idea was meant to be a twist on what happens when a Kindly One thinks s/he can build a freehold, and then places the characters within said-realm, only to have them realize that yeah, their freehold may be flawed, but it could be much, much worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T22:02:48-07:00","id":167568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/166347-sheogorath-s-changeling-courts?p=167128#post167128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I didn't CHOOSE the name for the courts. If you actually played the Elder Scrolls, then you'd know that's what they are called. I just find it a hypocracy that people're getting offended at me for not having background information on the subject, when they themselves have no background information on what I'm talking about (eg the game). Besides, from an ingame perspective, what member of the Gentry would care if something appeared crass or offensive? They're evil!</div> </div> </div> </div>Ignorance about a game and ignorance about real life are entirely different levels of gravity. For example, only one of those things can potentially cause harm to real, living people, and it's not my inability to recite the Song of the Dragonborn. But if you want to talk about the Gentry...<br /> <br /> Well, let's talk about what the Courts in changeling <i>are</i>. They're not merely political organizations- the Seasonal Courts are specifically constructed to hold back the influence of the Fae through a constant, deliberate exchange of power. You see, the Gentry have a hard time understanding things like selflessness, or ideologies, or principles, except as elements of a persona. They don't understand why someone would intentionally surrender control, which confuses them and makes it harder for them to hunt down the changelings. They also serve as support groups for the traumatized changelings, keeping them at relatively high Clarity and ensuring that someone goes looking for them if they go missing.<br /> <br /> Thus, any Gentry who tries to create a Court will, at best, create a foul mockery that possesses none of the benefits of a court while retaining all of its drawbacks (oaths of fealty, required duties, etc.). At worst, it'll just attract other Fae, who will want to pluck up their favorite changelings as they flee/are dragged to the false Court... which might be the point, but it doesn't seem like it's supposed to be.<br /> <br /> If you really want to go the Mania and Dementia route, though, I would suggest looking up some archaic philosophy on the personality, where dementia just meant any form of insanity or mental breakdown, and mania meant any sort of excitement or high levels of emotion. Perhaps build the Courts around the Clarity system, with the Mania court seeking to maintain the highest levels of Clarity as possible so they can explore the many strange elements of reality, and the Dementia court seeking to dive as low as possible without going completely bonkers to &quot;reveal&quot; the &quot;hidden truth&quot; behind &quot;reality&quot;. Create Contracts around madness and sanity, the flexibility of perception and the ways in which emotion and psychosis intersect. Turn it into something interesting that your players can work with, so that it can be the basis of a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T22:55:41-07:00","id":167594,"title":"","content":"The Mania and Dementia MrParaduo is talking about are just names to two halves of Sheogorath's domain, the Shivering Isles, which represent the two halves of his own insanity which <i>is</i> rooted in the archaic philosophy you speak of. Also a weird yin-yang thing going on with the residents.<br /> <br /> @MrParaduo<br /> The only part that wouldn't fly with the Gentry version of him is his creativity hat, but the obsession with trying to be would suit him just fine. Incidentally, how well versed are your players with the Elder Scrolls?<br /> <br /> *EDIT*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","user":"DoeMan","date":". 06-13-2014, 02:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","name":"DoeMan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-13T04:53:09-07:00","id":167752,"title":"","content":"To be honest, I wasn't planning on hosting a game for this, mostly because this is just a think tank I felt like sharing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T07:55:00-07:00","id":176995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/166347-sheogorath-s-changeling-courts?p=166415#post166415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could actually make Kindly Ones of all the Deadric Princes, if you think about it. God help me if I know the exact stats for each or any of them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well if they were changelings, I think the following courts would suit them perfectly.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sheogorath, Sanguine, Azura, Clavicus Vile - <b>Spring Court:</b> They primarily deal with desire, beauty, or pleasure<br /> <br /> <br /> Nocturnal, Mephala, Namira, - <b>Winter Court</b>: They're the most secretive and mysterious of the lot.<br /> <br /> <br /> Vaermina, Meridia, Peryite, Hermaeus Mora - <b>Autumn Court:</b> They seem to relate to magic and secret knowledge more than the others.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hircine, Molag Bal, Malacath, Boethiah, Mehrunes Dagon - <b>Summer Court:</b> The most violent of the Daedric lords","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-22-2014, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T08:50:14-07:00","id":177077,"title":"","content":"Daedric Princes certainly have a Gentry vibe to them, but they'd have to be de-powered a bit and changed pretty heavily to fit within the CtL Mythos. As Daedric Princes are not only literally the realms they inhabit, but are in fact those very concepts they represent. Sheogorath is Madness, he is in the mind of every mortal, and he represents more than mental derangements. He is the song that musicians feel within their souls, he is a the image in the mind which artists attempt to reveal to the world, and he is absolutely fucking terrifying. Not only can he make it rain animals over a major city that he conjured out of thin air, he can do things like shatter continents, or throw moons at cities he doesn't like. He can turn anything into anything else with a thought, unless it specifically has some innate resistance to it (ie a demigod or god). Individuals like Mehrunes Dagon command legions of immortal self-resurrecting soldiers who are all wearing soulforged armor and wielding powerful magics. Can't really do any of that in CtL without breaking the theme. Better to stick with being &quot;inspired&quot; by them, rather than trying to port them over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1604-oliver-the-bold","name":"Oliver the Bold","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T07:08:45-07:00","id":287576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You could actually make Kindly Ones of all the Deadric Princes, if you think about it. God help me if I know the exact stats for each or any of them. </div> </div> </div>Molag Bal would be definitely a scum even among Keepers, though, you know, even those Daedra deemed as good by Mer and Men are not to be crossed. Azura can be petty, vindictive bitch on a bad day.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-20T07:34:45-07:00","id":287610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/166347-sheogorath-s-changeling-courts?p=287576#post287576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Molag Bal would be definitely a scum even among Keepers, though, you know, even those Daedra deemed as good by Mer and Men are not to be crossed. Azura can be petty, vindictive bitch on a bad day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except for Peryite. Nobody takes that poor guy seriously. And he causes the plague. :'3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link"