n't say I'm impressed with the idea. At all. I'm disabled, and no, a game circling around that would not be amazing. In fact, it'd be something I'd slap someone over, because it's sure to be a piece of utterly inaccurate bull-hooey (even with research, because guess what? Mania and dementia develop and manifest themselves differently in different people!) and not to mention, well... Mania and dementia are real psychological conditions that real people suffer from, and they are not diametrically opposed. If you want to focus the courts on something other than the Seasons, you can do that, but don't bring real mental illness into it without at least knowing what you're talking about.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> In the elder scrolls game, Mania and Dementia do have recognizable differences. Those who belonged to the court of Mania were bright, exuberant, and generally enjoyed life's pleasures to the fullest, bordering on ecstatic levels. In contrast, those who joined the Court of Dementia were dark, melancholy and violent. Hell, the Duchess of Dementia appoints you her grand inquisitor so you can uncover a plot against her life, and your method of interrogation is to blast people with lightning!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T11:48:44-08:00","id":343128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like when 3 Elves betrayed her and she decided the best course of action was to destroy their 